Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
deflation.nb : dirac16complex with three deflating degrees of freedom x5, x6, \
x7\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"40e673e7-89f2-4553-8827-c8a90c7cf521"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook studies the primordial gravitational field of 6planes.nb in \
which the three superluminal-time directions x5, x6, x7 are replaced by \
DEFLATING degrees of freedom. The line element is
ds^2 = Tan[6 H x0]^2 dx0^2 + E^(-2 H x4) Sin[6 H x0]^(-1/3) (dx1^2 + dx2^2 + \
dx3^2) - dx4^2 - g55 dx5^2 - g66 dx6^2 - g77 dx7^2 ,
g55 = b55 Exp[-a x4], g66 = b66 Exp[-a x4], g77 = b77 Exp[-a x4], a > 0, b55 \
> 0, b66 > 0, b77 > 0.
x5, x6, x7 stay timelike (the signature remains (4,4) with eta = \
diag(+1,+1,+1,+1,-1,-1,-1,-1)), so the eight real 16x16 Dirac matrices \
(T16^A)[0..7] of Pre-gravity6plane.nb remain the Dirac matrices of \
dirac16complex. Every equation used is written in this notebook and every \
result is computed below; evaluate from top to bottom. Built on \
Pre-gravity6plane.nb by P. L. Nash ((C) 2022, GPL).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b9f7857-c814-4acb-aeab-db3c74a5f07f"],

Cell["Part 0. Coordinates and conventions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"430faefa-617b-49b4-bdbf-62249fdb15e3"],

Cell["\<\
The Cartesian coordinates of the project are X = {x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, \
x7}: x0 = hidden space, x1..x3 = 3-space, x4 = time, x5..x7 = superluminal \
(\"deflating\") time. The flat metric is eta4488 = \
diag(+1,+1,+1,+1,-1,-1,-1,-1), exactly as in Pre-gravity6plane.nb.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1e03fe4e-e30b-4fcc-a4da-2bc3f0f47580"],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];
X = {x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7};
eta4488 = ArrayFlatten[{{IdentityMatrix[4], 0}, {0, -IdentityMatrix[4]}}];
ID4 = IdentityMatrix[4]; ID8 = IdentityMatrix[8]; ID16 = IdentityMatrix[16];
Diagonal[eta4488]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"379b8a57-31ce-4c5c-831d-47bf8e804045"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1", ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]=",ExpressionUUID->"be20224a-2d0d-453f-b613-06bc24cf8400"],

Cell["Part 1. The eight real 16x16 Dirac matrices (T16^A)[0..7]", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a9353bd3-4be7-4e1e-9d6d-06cf98295415"],

Cell["1.1 Exact construction (identical to Pre-gravity6plane.nb)", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"075e2523-d4a0-4a5a-b9b3-205516311a14"],

Cell["\<\
Spinor metric sigma (8x8), self-dual (s4by4) and anti-self-dual (t4by4) 4x4 \
matrices, the six antisymmetric 8x8 matrices, tau[A], taubar[A] = \
sigma.Transpose[sigma.tau[A]], and finally (T16^A)[A] = [[0, taubar[A]], \
[tau[A], 0]]. In this notebook the symbol T16A[A] stands for (T16^A)[A] of \
Pre-gravity6plane.nb (the old notebook used the Notation package to make \
T16^A a symbol; here we use the plain name T16A to keep the notebook \
package-free).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7e38284-9ccc-4e95-ad11-44948d017620"],

Cell["\<\
sigma = ArrayFlatten[{{ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}], ID4}, {ID4, ConstantArray[0, \
{4, 4}]}}];
Qa[h_, p_, q_] := Signature[{h, p, q, 4}];
Qb[h_, p_, q_] := ID4[[p, 4]]*ID4[[q, h]] - ID4[[p, h]]*ID4[[q, 4]];
s4by4[h_] := Table[Qa[h, p, q] - Qb[h, p, q], {p, 4}, {q, 4}];   (* self-dual \
antisymmetric *)
t4by4[h_] := Table[Qa[h, p, q] + Qb[h, p, q], {p, 4}, {q, 4}];   (* \
anti-self-dual antisymmetric *)
sixAntiSymmetric8by8 = Flatten[{Table[ArrayFlatten[{{0, s4by4[h]}, {s4by4[h], \
0}}], {h, 1, 3}],
    Table[ArrayFlatten[{{0, t4by4[h]}, {-t4by4[h], 0}}], {h, 3, 1, -1}]}, 1];
tau[0] = ID8; Do[tau[h] = sixAntiSymmetric8by8[[h]], {h, 1, 6}];
tau[7] = tau[1].tau[2].tau[3].tau[4].tau[5].tau[6];
Do[taubar[h] = sigma.Transpose[sigma.tau[h]], {h, 0, 7}];
Do[T16A[A] = ArrayFlatten[{{0, taubar[A]}, {tau[A], 0}}], {A, 0, 7}];
T16A[8] = Dot @@ Table[T16A[A], {A, 0, 7}];          (* chirality  Gamma = T0 \
T1 ... T7 *)
sigma16 = T16A[0].T16A[1].T16A[2].T16A[3];           (* spinor metric of \
dirac16complex *)
PL = (ID16 - T16A[8])/2; PR = (ID16 + T16A[8])/2;    (* chiral projectors *)
SAB = Table[(T16A[A].T16A[B] - T16A[B].T16A[A])/4, {A, 0, 7}, {B, 0, 7}];
Gamma5 = T16A[8];
MatrixForm /@ Table[T16A[A], {A, 0, 7}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"638d55ea-86f1-45fe-b096-20fea9aef224"],

