Cell["\<\
Part 9. Pairs of +mass and -mass universes in the deflation field\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e5070549-d854-45b8-94bf-5c0508a79a28"],

Cell["\<\
(i) Mass-sign pairing: C psi = Gamma psi^* and P1 psi(x) = T^1 psi(R1 x) map \
solutions with mass +m onto solutions with mass -m (exact, Part 7). (ii) \
Frequency pairing: the field equation has real coefficients, so complex \
conjugation maps a mode of frequency omega onto one of frequency -omega. \
(iii) Mixing of the two mirror sectors: with K = -I sigma16.T^4, the \
Lagrangian has no cross terms between psi_+ and psi_- from the directions \
x0..x4, while the deflating directions x5, x6, x7 couple the sectors with the \
GROWING coefficients E^(a x4/2)/Sqrt[bjj]. Deflation therefore mixes +mass \
and -mass universes ever more strongly (Part 8, K=-1 fraction).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a4e7b745-d1c7-4575-b727-2bf1ac526ab9"],

Cell["\<\
crossD[A_] := Simplify[(ID16 + K).sigma16.(cD[[A + 1]] T16A[A]).(ID16 - K), \
assumD];
<|\"no + / - cross term from direction A (A = 0..7)\" -> \
Table[AllTrue[Flatten[crossD[A]], # === 0 &], {A, 0, 7}],
 \"magnitudes of the cross-term entries for A = 5, 6, 7\" -> \
Table[Union[Simplify[Abs[Flatten[crossD[A]]], assumD]], {A, 5, 7}]|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"91fea956-c6a0-4e5d-855a-91225368ded4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"no + / - cross term from direction A (A = 0..7)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "True", ",", "True", ",", "True", ",", "True", ",", "True", ",", "False",
       ",", "False", ",", "False"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"magnitudes of the cross-term entries for A = 5, 6, 7\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "x4"}], "2"]]}], 
         SqrtBox["b55"]]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "x4"}], "2"]]}], 
         SqrtBox["b66"]]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        FractionBox[
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
           FractionBox[
            RowBox[{"a", " ", "x4"}], "2"]]}], 
         SqrtBox["b77"]]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[16]=",ExpressionUUID->"d8a4f93b-4c93-4a1d-a56d-ae320dba8dbe"],

Cell["\<\
(iv) Exact pair creation: conservation of the Krein charge. A mode of the \
pure deflation field (and every frozen-coefficient mode of Part 8) obeys chi' \
= M chi with M = T^4 (I Sum_(A != 4) kappa_A T^A - m), kappa_A = c_A k_A \
real. Because M^dagger K + K M = 0, the Krein charge Q = chi^dagger K chi = \
P+ - P- is conserved; here P+ and P- are the weights of the +mass (K = +1) \
and -mass (K = -1) sectors, and Q is the x4-component of the conserved \
current psibar gamma^mu psi of dirac16complex (sigma16.T^4 = I K, gamma^4 = \
T^4). The norm N = P+ + P- changes only through M^dagger + M = 2 I T^4 \
(kappa_5 T^5 + kappa_6 T^6 + kappa_7 T^7), i.e. only through the deflating \
directions, and this generator anticommutes with K: it creates +mass and \
-mass weight together. Hence P+ = (N + Q)/2 and P- = (N - Q)/2 grow by \
exactly the same amount: deflation creates {+mass, -mass} universes in pairs \
(numerically Q = 1 to within 2.2*10^-7 at x4 = -8, 0, x4*, 3, 5, and the K = \
-1 fraction equals (N - 1)/(2 N) to within 7.2*10^-7 on the grid x4 = -8, -7, \
..., 5; Part 8).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e6819762-f7a3-43b0-bc80-23e5a7477ffb"],

Cell["\<\
kapA = {kap0, kap1, kap2, kap3, 0, kap5, kap6, kap7};      (* kappa_A = c_A \
k_A : arbitrary real numbers *)
Mdef = T16A[4].(I Sum[kapA[[A + 1]] T16A[A], {A, 0, 7}] - m ID16);
MdefH = ComplexExpand[ConjugateTranspose[Mdef]];         (* all symbols real *)
<|\"sigma16.T^4 == I K\" -> (sigma16.T16A[4] === I K),
 \"M^dagger K + K M == 0 (Krein charge chi^dagger K chi conserved)\" -> \
(Simplify[MdefH.K + K.Mdef] === ConstantArray[0, {16, 16}]),
 \"M^dagger + M == 2 I T^4 (kap5 T^5 + kap6 T^6 + kap7 T^7)\" -> \
(Simplify[MdefH + Mdef - 2 I T16A[4].(kap5 T16A[5] + kap6 T16A[6] + kap7 \
T16A[7])] === ConstantArray[0, {16, 16}]),
 \"the norm-changing generator anticommutes with K\" -> (Simplify[K.(MdefH + \
Mdef) + (MdefH + Mdef).K] === ConstantArray[0, {16, 16}])|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ec93eb52-9471-4095-8317-0a485bbb6512"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"sigma16.T^4 == I K\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"M^dagger K + K M == 0 (Krein charge chi^dagger K chi \
conserved)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"M^dagger + M == 2 I T^4 (kap5 T^5 + kap6 T^6 + kap7 T^7)\"\>",
     "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"the norm-changing generator anticommutes with K\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "True"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"7428e9da-beae-4561-9942-d7e6c73b86b0"],

Cell["Part 10. Results", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cfd16803-ee39-4fb6-bd47-d9c0688eaddb"],

Cell["\<\
1. Metric and proper sizes (Part 4): the deflating degrees of freedom x5, x6, \
x7 have metric components -g55, -g66, -g77 with gjj = bjj E^(-a x4), proper \
sizes Sqrt[bjj] E^(-a x4/2) per unit coordinate interval, deflation rate d ln \
L/dx4 = -a/2 and e-folding time 2/a; Sqrt|g| = Sqrt[b55 b66 b77] Tan[6Hx0] \
Sin[6Hx0]^(-1/2) E^(-3(H + a/2) x4).
2. Curvature (Part 5): the Ricci scalar, the Einstein tensor and the \
Kretschmann scalar of the full field are computed exactly; the only non-zero \
off-diagonal Ricci component is R_04 = -3 H^2 Cot[6Hx0], it does not contain \
a, and G_04 = R_04. All of them depend on x0 only, not on x4, so deflation \
creates no curvature singularity at any finite x4. Near x0 = 0, R = -7/(108 \
H^2 x0^4) and R_abcd R^abcd = 85/(69984 H^4 x0^8) to leading order, \
independent of a: the curvature singularity at x0 = 0 of the primordial field \
remains. The pure deflation field is flat R^4 (x0..x3) times the block (x4, \
x5, x6, x7), which is maximally symmetric, R_abcd = (a^2/4)(g_ac g_bd - g_ad \
g_bc): with w = (2/a) E^(a x4/2) and yj = Sqrt[bjj] xj its metric is \
-(4/a^2)(dw^2 + dy5^2 + dy6^2 + dy7^2)/w^2, the hyperbolic 4-space H^4 of \
radius 2/a with all four directions timelike. Hence R = 3 a^2, R_abcd R^abcd \
= 3 a^4/2 and G^mu_mu = -3a^2/2 (mu = 0..3), -3a^2/4 (mu = 4..7) are \
constant.
3. Geodesics (Part 6): a world line with momentum p5 along a deflating \
direction has dx5/dlambda = -(p5/b55) E^(a x4) and (dx4/dlambda)^2 = 1 - \
(p5^2/b55) E^(a x4); it turns back at x4* = (1/a) Log[b55/p5^2]. In the \
hyperbolic block it is a semicircle of radius w* = 2 Sqrt[b55]/(a |p5|) \
standing on w = 0, with its top at x4*.
4. Field equation of dirac16complex (exact Grassmann derivation, Part 7): \
Cot[6Hx0] T^0 d0 psi + E^(H x4) Sin[6Hx0]^(1/6) Sum_i T^i d_i psi + T^4 d4 \
psi + E^(a x4/2) Sum_j T^j d_j psi/Sqrt[bjj] - (3/2) H Cot[6Hx0]^2 T^0 psi - \
(3/2)(H + a/2) T^4 psi = (m + lam psibar psi) psi; gamma^mu is covariantly \
constant, the Lagrangian is real, and the mass-sign maps C and P1 hold. The \
rescaling psi = Sin[6Hx0]^(1/4) E^(3(a + 2H) x4/4) chi removes both friction \
terms exactly (Part 8).
5. Universes (Part 8): omega^2 = m^2 + Cot[6Hx0]^2 k0^2 + E^(2Hx4) \
Sin[6Hx0]^(1/3) Sum k_i^2 - E^(a x4) Sum q_j^2/bjj. For k_i = 0, omega^2 \
decreases strictly and vanishes only at x4* = (1/a) Log[(m^2 + Cot[6Hx0]^2 \
k0^2)/Sum q_j^2/bjj], where the universe turns from oscillating to \
exponentially growing. The critical deflation rate is a_c = 2H; at a = 2H the \
late-time sign of omega^2 is that of Sin[6Hx0]^(1/3) Sum k_i^2 - Sum \
q_j^2/bjj. The exact numerical evolution (a = b55 = k = m = 1, q = 1/2, x4* = \
Log 8 = 2.0794) confirms it: the norm chi^dagger chi is 1 at x4 = -8, 1.0674 \
at x4 = 0, 1.9673 at x4*, 10.010 at x4 = 3, 1198.2 at x4 = 4 and 1.0588*10^7 \
at x4 = 5.
6. Pairs (Parts 8-9): directions x0..x4 produce no cross terms between the \
+mass and -mass sectors, while the deflating directions couple them with the \
growing coefficients E^(a x4/2)/Sqrt[bjj]. The Krein charge Q = P+ - P- = \
chi^dagger K chi is exactly conserved (M^dagger K + K M = 0), and the norm N \
= P+ + P- changes only through the deflating directions, by a generator that \
anticommutes with K. Therefore the +mass weight P+ = (N + Q)/2 and the -mass \
weight P- = (N - Q)/2 grow by exactly the same amount. In the example Q = 1 \
(the values computed at x4 = -8, 0, x4*, 3, 5 deviate from 1 by less than \
2.2*10^-7); P- = 1.2*10^-31, 0.0337, 0.4836, 4.5051, 5.293976*10^6 and P+ = \
1, 1.0337, 1.4836, 5.5051, 5.293977*10^6 at x4 = -8, 0, x4*, 3, 5. The K = -1 \
fraction, equal to (N - 1)/(2N) within 7.2*10^-7, is 1.2*10^-31 at x4 = -8, \
0.0316 at x4 = 0, 0.2458 at x4*, 0.4501 at x4 = 3 and 0.49999995 at x4 = 5. \
Deflation creates {+mass, -mass} universes in pairs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d28c7d44-0803-4d7d-997b-e910ea99006e"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
